      "writtenOn": "2026-05-20T09:37:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The original code reads host_mc-\u003ecount as the min_pages parameter for refill_memcache(). As we will copy the host_mc to tmp_mc to access the mc, move the tmp_mc here so that the count can be read from the tmp_mc.\n\nAh, good point.\n\n\u003e Maybe this is not important, we can just use READ_ONCE(host_mc-\u003ecount) if we prefer having tmp_mc in refill_memcache() for better reusability?\n\nYeah, seems so. In particular, then we can reuse it for the IOMMU\u0027s `refill_domain_memcache()` (which would just similarly use READ_ONCE(host_mc-\u003ecount) when calling this generic `refill_memcache()`).",
      "parentUuid": "281fc6b1_0e3e823e",
      "revId": "dc845c65ef8dc55ff4e31e5422eb28fef88e5a8f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
