      "message": "Hmm, late thought: can\u0027t we just use `*(volatile struct pkvm_memcache *)host_mc` (instead of relying on memcpy in a non-obvious way)?\n\n...BTW @willdeacon@google.com @tabba@google.com @qperret@google.com FYI here we are trying to address a potential TOCTOU which seems to exist in the ARM\u0027s `refill_memcache()` as well, due to `tmp \u003d *host_mc` which could be implemented by the compiler as multiple loads of the same data (IOW, due to the lack of an effective READ_ONCE).",
